{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## FIX LANDED LOCALLY — commit `2fe9a3313c04` (NOT pushed; operator lands + deploys)\n\nWorktree `/Users/joeoakhart/f643-verify-event-loop`, branched from `origin/main` at\n`8e2e3893e904` — the same tree as the deployed container `rebar-mcp-8e2e3893e904-8093`, so the\ninvestigation ran against exactly the build that produced the report.\n\n### The fix\n\nOne guard at the top of `PydanticAIRunner.run` (`runner.py:369`): if a loop is running on this\nthread, re-enter `run` on a worker that has none. Two new helpers in `model_classes.py` (the\nmodule that already owns rebar's event-loop lifecycle): `event_loop_running()` and\n`drive_off_event_loop()`, the latter dispatching through a fresh `contextvars.copy_context()`.\n\n`RUNNERS = (\"pydantic_ai\", \"fake\")` and `FakeRunner` drives no loop, so `PydanticAIRunner.run` is\nthe **sole** real drive — the single guard gives every surface (CLI, MCP, library facade,\nautomated callers) the same protection, and covers all six sync-drive sites at once, including\n`providers.py:336`'s `asyncio.run(client.aclose())` teardown, which was failing on **every** MCP\nrun and being swallowed at `:337` (leaking the connection pool).\n\nAlso corrected `_mcp_health.py`'s docstring, which asserted that sync MCP tools run on\n`anyio.to_thread` workers. They do not. That false belief is what let this ship.\n\n**This is a restoration, not new behaviour.** The pre-migration runner carried this exact guard —\n`75e598a41e7c^:runner.py:405-434` probed `asyncio.get_running_loop()` and fell back to a\none-worker `ThreadPoolExecutor` \"so this works even when the caller is already inside a running\nevent loop\". The pydantic-ai migration dropped it (see the RCA comment above).\n\n### RED -> GREEN -> mutation\n\n`tests/unit/test_runner_running_event_loop.py` (6 tests). Every one drives the runner from inside\n`asyncio.run(...)`, so a future \"fix\" that only works without a running loop leaves them red.\n\n- **RED first, for the right reason** — before any fix:\n  `LLMUnavailableError: the LLM provider call failed: This event loop is already running` (3 failed,\n  2 passed: the no-loop path and the sync-MCP-tool premise, which is the asymmetry being fixed).\n- **GREEN against a held-out oracle** — the test file was moved OUT of the tree before the fix was\n  written; the implementing agent never saw it. Restored afterwards: **6 passed**.\n- **Mutation M1 (defect re-seeded)** — disable the guard: back to **3 failed** with the original\n  error. Run under `sandbox-exec` with writes denied outside the worktree.\n- **Mutation M2 (contextvars dropped)** — `pool.submit(context.run, ...)` -> `pool.submit(...)`:\n  initially **SURVIVED**, a real hole in my own suite. Without `copy_context` the gate-session vars\n  are absent in the worker and `assert_gated` fails closed on every *agentic* run — invisible to the\n  other tests because the offline `model_override` harness is exempt from `assert_gated`. Added\n  `test_the_gate_session_survives_the_hop_off_the_event_loop`, which pins it against the real\n  `gate_context` vars; M2 now returns RED.\n\n### Replication of the reported shape\n\nDriving a `single_turn`/`structured` call — the exact shape of the step that died — through a real\nin-process FastMCP server as a sync `@mcp.tool` (so the body genuinely runs on the loop thread):\n\n    {\"verify_failed\": false, \"verify_error\": null, \"verify_requests\": 1, \"verifications\": 1}\n\nagainst the reported `verify_failed: true`, `verify_error: \"...This event loop is already running\"`,\n`verify_requests: 0`.\n\n### Gates\n\n    make lint                                  -> pass\n    make typecheck                             -> Success: no issues found in 679 source files\n    pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py -> 4 passed   (runner.py 785/800, model_classes.py 595/800)\n    scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check -> active=40 new=0 increased=0 stale=9\n      (.github/complexity-baseline.json untouched; PydanticAIRunner.run 22 -> 23 against its ceiling of 24)\n    pytest tests/unit                          -> 14051 passed, 51 skipped\n    the async-context risk surface (13 files that combine an async context with the LLM runner)\n                                               -> 328 passed, 27 skipped\n\nThe full-suite run also reported 2 errors in `test_code_review_public_exposure.py` — both\nself-inflicted by running the suite concurrently with my own commit (\"The repo HEAD moved during\nthis test 8e2e3893e9 -> 2fe9a3313c\" and a `.tickets-trac...` temp dir appearing). Re-run on a quiet\ntree: **5 passed**. Not a regression.\n\n### NOT DONE — deliberately\n\n- **The LIVE VALIDATION criterion is NOT satisfied and NOT ticked.** It needs the deployed server;\n  the operator lands and deploys. No acceptance criteria were ticked and the ticket is left\n  `in_progress`.\n- **No `caused_by` link.** Refused because story `7d58-e88b-1643-4542` predates the `rebar-ticket:`\n  trailer convention and so has no commit referencing it. Overriding needs `--force`, which agents\n  are prohibited from using. Operator action wanted (see the RCA comment for the exact invocation).\n- **No plan-review attestation run.** Neither Gerrit bugfix-size escalation signal fires: the diff\n  is **69 non-test lines** against the 150-line floor, and none of the three touched files has ≥2\n  prior bug-fix commits on `origin/main` in the last 7 days (measured: 0, 0, 0). Nothing consumes an\n  attestation for this change, and the claim succeeded without one — so a 15-20 minute billable run\n  was skipped as unwarranted rather than as an oversight. Say the word if you want it anyway.\n\n### Store health (pre-existing, operator-facing)\n\n`rebar fsck` reports `PUSH_PENDING: local 'tickets' branch is ahead of origin/tickets by 24\ncommit(s)` — every ticket write in this session (including this comment) is committed locally but\n**not pushed**; retries keep losing a race with a concurrent writer. It also reports\n`ENV_ID_MISMATCH` naming 2 other environment ids, \"the signature of a tracker re-clone that did not\ncarry over its git-ignored local state\" — consistent with `7be0edb7132d fix(mcp): re-clone an\nunusable tickets store`. Consequence worth knowing: op-cert attestations signed under those\nidentities verify as `foreign_key` here and must be re-earned. I did not touch the store beyond the\nwritebacks this protocol prescribes.\n\n### Discovered work\n\n`wounded-resident-bushbaby` (`b580-98b6-d9b7-4817`), linked `discovered_from` this bug: the MCP\ngraceful-drain / zero-downtime-deploy contract in ADR 0104 and ADR 0079 rests on the same false\npremise this bug disproved. Filed as an explicitly UNPROVEN lead with the experiment that would\nsettle it — this fix may have incidentally repaired it, and I did not verify either way.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787881527535308870,"uuid":"16dfd164-1ca2-4ef3-867c-660a428a71c4"}